{{DRN archive top|Closed as failed.  Excessively lengthy discussion was unable to narrow the issues down to a limited number of alternatives.  A [[WP:RFC|Request for Comments]] with a large number of alternatives was then launched, but the responses were that the RFC would not be constructive, and the RFC is being cancelled.  It is clear that several editors are dissatisfied with the current methodology, but they have provided long statements that are too verbose to be a useful basis for formulating an RFC.  Resume discussion on the article talk page.  A new request can be made for discussion here leading to the formulation of a new RFC if the discussion identifies no more than two alternatives.  [[User:Robert McClenon|Robert McClenon]] ([[User talk:Robert McClenon|talk]]) 17:42, 14 February 2026 (UTC)}}
<span style="font-size:110%">'''Have you discussed this on a talk page?'''</span>

Yes, I have discussed this issue on a talk page already.

